---
/* EVENT — register hero, direction A "Pinned" (sketches/register-hero-A.png,
  spec in sketches/SKETCH_PROMPTS_REGISTER_HERO.md).

  Two columns: the client's actual flyer, matted and pinned, on the left; the
  site's own voice plus the form on the right.

  Why the flyer is matted rather than placed bare: measured, its background is
  #1A1A1A against the site's dark ground #120D0B -- 1.09:1, so on a dark
  section it would have no edge at all and read as a broken image. It sits on
  the EMBER ground instead, inside a paper mat with a hairline, which is the
  "real border" the sketch calls for.

  Why the site repeats NO BUSHELS / the date / the venue as live type when the
  flyer already shows them: the flyer is a raster. It says nothing to a screen
  reader or to a search engine, and SC3 makes the date, theme and register CTA
  this page's number-one job. The flyer SHOWS them; the type STATES them. */
---
<section class="ev g-ember" id="event" data-fade>

  <div class="ev__hero">

    <!-- LEFT: the real flyer, pinned. Tilt is 2deg at rest; it arrives at 6deg
         and settles (conference-behaviour.js). One tilt on the page, nothing
         else is off-axis. -->
    <figure class="ev__flyer" id="evFlyer">
      <div class="ev__flyerMat">
        <img src="/img/flyer-no-bushels.webp" width="900" height="1125"
             alt="No Bushels, a Christian creative conference presented by The Glow Tribe. Saturday 21 November 2026, Warri, Delta State. Free entry, registration required."
             decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
      </div>
    </figure>

    <!-- RIGHT: the site's own voice, then the ask -->
    <div class="ev__ask">
      <h1 class="ev__title">NO<br>BUSHELS</h1>
      <p class="ev__meta"><span>21 NOV 2026</span><span>EU Centre, Warri</span></p>

      <div class="ev__flip" id="regFlip">
        <form class="ev__form ev__face ev__face--front" id="regForm">
          <p class="ev__k">Register</p>
          <div class="field"><label for="rn2">Name</label><input id="rn2" type="text" autocomplete="name" required></div>
          <div class="field"><label for="re2">Email</label><input id="re2" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></div>
          <div class="field"><label for="rp2">Phone</label><input id="rp2" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required></div>
          <div class="field"><label for="rd2">Creative discipline</label>
            <select id="rd2" required>
              <option value="" disabled selected>Choose one</option>
              <option>Music</option><option>Film</option><option>Writing</option>
              <option>Photography</option><option>Design</option><option>Other</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <button class="submit" id="regSubmit" type="submit">Register · it's free</button>
          <p class="ev__small note">⚠ Backend not wired · submissions are not stored.</p>
        </form>

        <!-- the reverse. Not a message appended below the form — the same panel,
             turned over. -->
        <div class="ev__face ev__face--back" id="regBack" aria-hidden="true">
          <p class="ev__k">You're in</p>
          <p class="ev__backHead">See you on the<br><em>21<sup>st</sup></em></p>
          <p class="ev__backText">Directions and a reminder will reach you by email. Bring whatever
             you're working on, however unfinished.</p>
          <p class="ev__backMeta">EU Centre, Warri · Doors 09:00</p>
          <button class="ev__undo" type="button">← Register someone else</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The connector: a slanted dotted arrow running from the flyer down to
         the register button, so the poster and the ask read as one sentence.
         Decorative only -- the relationship is already carried by DOM order
         and by the form's own label, so this is hidden from assistive tech.
         Desktop only: once the columns stack, the diagonal has nothing to
         span and would point at the wrong thing. -->
    <svg class="ev__link" viewBox="0 0 200 150" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <path class="ev__linkPath"
            d="M6 10 C 70 34, 118 60, 160 108"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4"
            stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray="1 11"/>
      <path class="ev__linkHead"
            d="M146 100 L 165 115 L 142 119"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4"
            stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </svg>

  </div>

</section>
